[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table disagrees once the page renders, and
the reports split once more when you read them. Each problem below has a ticket of its own.
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} {outcome} />

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser read every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so day and month came out swapped: "Booked for 2 December. The invite says 12 February."
Fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

**`hint`: booking-v3 told day-first tenants to type the month first.** Its date field printed
`MM/DD/YYYY`. People typed what it said, and the form read the date the tenant's way, day first.
The parser fix did not touch this path. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so the path is gone.

**`one-day`: invites and reminders show the day before.** "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." The date keeps its month and loses a day, which no day/month swap
can do; it looks like a time zone shift. The desk read these reports as one-day moves
(`desk-notes.json`) but files them under `parser` by tenant. The parser fix cannot move a date by one
day, and the engineering update does not mention them. Nothing in the kb explains them yet.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed with the parser fix, and the hint problem ends with the booking-v3 form. The one-day
reports have no fix and no explanation. If another one comes in, reopen its ticket; do not merge it
into parser.
</Callout>

## How this was counted

- From `reports-4471.json`: one report per id (`uniqueById`), because the export pages overlap.
- The desk's way: every report counts where #4471's cause table files it, by the tenant's locale,
  booking form and channel (`causes.ts`). The one-day reports come from the desk's own notes and
  count under `parser` as well.
- Intake tags are not used. They follow the reporter's browser, not the tenant.
- The table is built from the exported data at render time, so it follows the next export.

## For the desk

- Before you mark a big ticket known, render its page and read the cause table, not the paragraph above it.
- Subject lines do not tell these problems apart (see the note under the table). Decision 0001 still
  says to merge on subject; a new decision record has to replace it. This page does not.

